## 6. Project discipline (apply to any future work)
1. **Dependency-first**: write the real dependency, never a stub to
   unblock compilation. If only one file from a later phase is
   needed, write only that file (mirror.c precedent).
2. **Audit-before-fix**: on any failure, determine root cause
   (implementation bug / contract mismatch / test error) before
   changing anything. Quote exact lines, don't summarize from memory.
3. **No invented constants**: thresholds, formulas, protocol
   defaults all need a citation (RFC, existing code, or explicit
   human decision) or an honest `NOT_CALIBRATED`/`UNKNOWN` marker.
4. **"Mismatch" ≠ "contradiction"**: two things looking inconsistent
   needs investigation before being called broken — there may be a
   valid reason (e.g. different callers, different contracts).
